The issue is in `app/service.py`. The generated protobuf message `user_pb2.User` has a field named `emial` (misspelled) in the `.proto` file:

```proto
message User {
  int64 id = 1;
  string name = 2;
  string emial = 3;
  Role role = 4;
}
```

However, in `app/service.py`, the `make_user` function attempts to set a field named `email`:

```python
def make_user(uid, name, email, role=user_pb2.MEMBER):
    return user_pb2.User(id=uid, name=name, email=email, role=role)
```

The error message `ValueError: Protocol message User has no "email" field` indicates that the Python code is trying to set `email`, but the generated message class expects `emial`.

I need to fix the `make_user` function in `app/service.py` to use `emial` instead of `email`.

